# evidence/ is NOT ignored: history.jsonl is the point of the repository.
# evidence/refutations.jsonl is written by `make refute` and IS committed: a repository that
# invites refutation should show the refutations it has already survived. It never backs a
# published number either way.

# Coverage's data file, written by `make fast` on every run. It was COMMITTED on 7 September
# 2026, in the commit that added the coverage gate, and a tracked file that a lane rewrites is
# not a small untidiness:
#
#   * `git status --porcelain` reported " M .coverage" after the first command in the README,
#     `_code_changes` in generator/seeds.py excludes only the evidence directory, so every
#     record written after `make fast` carried `tree_dirty: true` and the front page said "on an
#     uncommitted tree". That is the same condition the long comment in seeds.py describes as
#     having emptied that field of meaning once already, nine records out of ten;
#   * and in a second clone it aborted `git checkout main` outright with "Your local changes
#     would be overwritten by checkout", which is a tool's scratch space blocking a branch
#     change in somebody else's checkout.
#
# tests/fast/test_seeds.py asserts that nothing the fast lane writes is tracked, so this cannot
# come back by being added again.
.coverage
.coverage.*

# `npm install` in the mermaid step of .github/workflows/fast.yml writes it here. Nothing
# in this repository is a node package; the directory is a tool's scratch space, and an
# untracked one is enough to make `git status --porcelain` call the tree dirty.
node_modules/
